      <div type="clause" n="20.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 20.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 20.2" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="560" ed="#liebermann"/>Archiepiscopi, episcopi, comites<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.18"/> et alie potestates<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.g"/> in terris<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.h"/> proprii potentatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.19"/> sui sacam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.20"/> et socnam habent, tol<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.21"/> et theam et infongenþeaf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.22"/> — in ceteris uero, per empcionem uel cambicionem uel quoquo modo perquisitis, socam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.23"/> et sacam habent in causis communibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.24"/> et halimotis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.25"/> pertinentibus — super<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.i"/> suos et in suo et aliquando super alterius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.i"/> homines, presertim si in forisfaciendo retenti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="k" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.k"/> uel grauati<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.26"/> fuerint; et illic competentem emendationem habeant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.27"/>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 560 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">jedenfalls</hi> Äbte, <hi rend="italic">vielleicht alle</hi> barones in capite tenentes, <hi rend="italic">im Gegensatz zu</hi> uauasores 27; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Maitland</hi> Domesday 81</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in any case abbots, perhaps all barones in capite tenentes, in contrast to uauasores 27; cf. Maitland Domesday 81</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Amtsterritorien <hi rend="italic">im Gegensatz zu</hi> persönlichem Eigen; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Inst. Cn. III 58, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">territories held by virtue of office, in contrast to personal property; cf. Inst. Cn. III 58, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">wiederholt</hi> 27; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 81, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">repeated 27; cf. 81, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.k" n="k" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">auf der That verhaftet oder sofort in Anklage versetzt; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 27&lt;sup&gt;<hi rend="italic">m</hi>&lt;/sup&gt;</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">arrested in the act or immediately accused; cf. 27&lt;sup&gt;<hi rend="italic">m</hi>&lt;/sup&gt;</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K Co Or Gi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in K Co Or Gi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">potestatis <hi rend="italic">Lond; danach ändern</hi> propriæ <hi rend="italic">und</hi> suæ <hi rend="italic">Edd.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">potestatis Lond; accordingly Edd. alter propriæ and suæ</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sacham et socham <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sacham et socham Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">thol <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thol Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">infangenþef <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">infangenþef Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">socham et sacham <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">socham et sacham Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">omnibus <hi rend="italic">ändert Wi gegen Hss.; so Tho.</hi> [<hi rend="italic">aber vgl.</hi> 19, 2]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wi alters to omnibus against the MSS; so Tho. [but cf. 19, 2]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hallem. <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> halem. <hi rend="italic">Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hallem. Sc; halem. Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">crau. <hi rend="italic">empfiehlt Somner</hi> [<hi rend="italic">allein für</hi> crafian <hi rend="italic">steht</hi> grau. <hi rend="italic">auch</hi> 27]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Somner recommends crau. [but grau. stands for crafian in 27 too]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">560</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hāt <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hāt Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht die Gerichtsbarkeit (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 37. 38) heisst gekauft (gegen Maitland <hi rend="italic">Domesday</hi> 82), sondern: der nur hinzu erworbene (nicht als Amtsland [<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3] oder Stamm-Baronie verwaltete oder ererbte) Grundbesitz bringt dem Baron nur gewöhnliche (nicht höhere) Gerichtsbarkeit</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It is not the jurisdiction (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 37. 38) that is called purchased (against Maitland <hi rend="italic">Domesday</hi> 82); rather, landed property merely acquired in addition (not administered as official land [<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3] or as an ancestral barony, nor inherited) brings the baron only ordinary (not higher) jurisdiction</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_20-2.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl infangenþeof</hi> 2. 3. 5; Anefang 28a; Privileg 3a. Regulär gilt Beschränkung auf eigene Untertanen, wie bei ECf retr. und Bracton; die Unbeschränktheit kann bis <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">wite aliquando</hi> gehen; <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 27.—<hi rend="italic">Item. Arch</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">potestatus</hi>{19} <hi rend="italic">s. s. et socam h., thol</hi>—<hi rend="italic">infangeneþief</hi>—<hi rend="italic">crauati</hi>{26} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl infangenþeof</hi> 2. 3. 5; Anefang 28a; Privileg 3a. As a rule a restriction to one's own subjects applies, as in ECf retr. and Bracton; the absence of restriction can extend as far as <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">wite aliquando</hi>; <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 27.—<hi rend="italic">Item. Arch</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">potestatus</hi>{19} <hi rend="italic">s. s. et socam h., thol</hi>—<hi rend="italic">infangeneþief</hi>—<hi rend="italic">crauati</hi>{26} Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
